  "rationale": "Only mfa_admin and mfa_dbadmin are deployed. Nothing is patched, the network is not segmented and mfa_user is off, so the attacker gets well inside but stops short of the data stores. Reachable path: exploit_web gives foothold_web. pivot_internal works because the network is not segmented, giving reach_internal. steal_user_cred gives stolen_user. auth_appserver/apiserver/ciserver work because mfa_user is off, giving those footholds. kerberoast gives stolen_admin. escalate_ciserver works because ciserver is unpatched, giving admin_ciserver, and leak_secrets_ciserver then gives stolen_dbadmin. The block: auth_dc and auth_adfs both require NOT mfa_admin, so admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). That condition is false because mfa_dbadmin is deployed and neither admin_dc nor admin_adfs is reachable. No other technique gives foothold_db, foothold_fileserver or foothold_backup. Without those footholds, admin_db, admin_fileserver and admin_backup are unreachable, so all three exfiltrate techniques stay blocked and exfiltrated never becomes true."
